],[28889,7.9,2012,46,118,28],[28890,9.4,1954,48,113,24],[28891,16.3,1954,55,114,22],[28892,24.4,1954,59,118,22]],"links":[["Washakie County in the Farmland Atlas","/farmland-atlas/wyoming/washakie-county"],["ARC or PLC in Washakie County","/arc-plc/wyoming/washakie-county"],["PRF calculator","/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 17 grids runs 75 years from 1951 to 2025, and April to May and October to November each came in under 90% of normal in 38 of those years. In 2025, the middle of the grids got 41% of normal in November to December and 58% in August to September. So far in 2026, May to June sits at 43% on the middle of the grids. Grid 28589 had its driest year in 1954 at 38%.</p>"}
